// mem_checkpoint — SELF-HOSTED `mem.save` / `mem.restore` (#1423 stage 4): the
// C-041 arena-checkpoint pair on the wasm legs. v0's wasm leg saved and reset a
// bump pointer; v1's RC discipline reclaims scratch deterministically at scope
// end, so — exactly like native (runtime/rs/src/mem.rs: save() = 0, restore() =
// no-op, the allocator manages memory) — the trivial pair IS the implementation.
// Same shape as bytes.heap_save / bytes.heap_restore (stdlib/bytes_core.almd):
// the checkpoint is OPAQUE (never printed) and post-restore results are
// identical by construction on every leg. Parity evidence:
// spec/wasm_cross/mem_checkpoint.almd.
fn mem_save() -> Int = 0

fn mem_restore(mark: Int) -> Unit = ()
